From 965c3877458eddf74f7258753cf6c09528005295 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 03:04:17 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Path task P: trajectory objective with snap rejection,
 targets P1/P2, baselines, batch

- traj_opt: Objective classes (TerminalShape for S, MidTracking for P);
  Evaluator(objective=, reject_snap=): a snap-flagged step makes the
  rollout infeasible (L-BFGS f=+inf, Adam reverts); per-step adjoint.
- path_tracking: reference paths and the one-step DLS tracker with the
  exact mid-node sensitivity (designed motion and greedy baseline).
- train_path.py: targets/inits/check/train/greedy/jobs/report/figure/verify,
  as train_shape.py; snap-free calibrated common initialization.
- configs: task_path_peg_3d (P1, one peg, untwisted start) and
  task_path_pegs2_3d (P2, two pegs); default keys.
- run_path_batch.sh: the whole batch of one target.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018dBMfu4YMay4NhBK2t2Grp
